  @ ------------------------------------------------------------
  @  TriAsymAll
  @  Everything about one point, tagged: CDF, PDF, CDFc, mean, deviation.
  @  Author & design          : Jean Wilson
  @  Co-authors & programming  : Claude & Claude Code (Anthropic)
  @  Arguments may be given loose or bundled in a list of 4; that list is
  @  what LastArguments reports, and its length is checked before use.
  @ ------------------------------------------------------------
  IF DUP TypeName "list" == THEN IF DUP Size 4 ≠ THEN "TriAsymAll: needs 4 arguments" DoError END Explode Drop END
  → Xminv Xmaxv xpv Xv « Xminv 0 + Xmaxv 0 + xpv 0 + Xv 0 + → Xmin Xmax xp X « 'IFTE(X≤Xmin;0;IFTE(X≤xp;((X-Xmin)^2)/((Xmax-Xmin)*(xp-Xmin));IFTE(X≤Xmax;1-((Xmax-X)^2)/((Xmax-Xmin)*(Xmax-xp));1)))' →Num 'Kc' STO Kc "CDF" →Tag 'IFTE(X<Xmin;0;IFTE(X≤xp;2*(X-Xmin)/((Xmax-Xmin)*(xp-Xmin));IFTE(X≤Xmax;2*(Xmax-X)/((Xmax-Xmin)*(Xmax-xp));0)))' →Num "PDF" →Tag '1-Kc' →Num "CDFc" →Tag '(Xmin+Xmax+xp)/3' →Num "μ" →Tag '√((Xmin^2+Xmax^2+xp^2-Xmin*Xmax-Xmin*xp-Xmax*xp)/18)' →Num "sx" →Tag { Kc } PURGE Xminv Xmaxv xpv Xv 4 →List Drop » »
